  "body": "The steps for *Traverse history by a delta* https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#traverse-the-history-by-a-delta seem to assume only a single browsing context will be traversed.\r\n\r\nIn the case of a delta > 1, multiple browsing contexts may be traversed to a different document. In this case, it is not clear what the _specified browsing context_ should be.\r\n\r\nShould each browsing context that is being traversed prompt its active document to unload?\r\nIf so, what should happen if one document is allowed to unload, but not the other?\r\n\r\nI have created a page to test this behavior across multiple browsers https://servo-experiments.surge.sh/beforeunload-parent.html\r\n\r\ncc @asajeffrey @gterzian",
